  ],
  "reproduction_outputs": "Ignored build/events-profile contains the source variants, release objects/executables, and individual stdout/stderr logs. Normal bench/results/versus.jsonl is not modified by this script.",
  "variants": {
    "baseline": "Original generated event behavior with phase clock instrumentation.",
    "event_first": "Move TIDE_CMD_EVENT to a conditional before the native apply-loop kind switch, removing its switch case. Preserves ordering and behavior, but did not show a clear improvement.",
    "no_clear": "Diagnostic hot-path queue insertion omits memset. Queue page changes still use normal tide_queue_push_page. Unsafe for general commands/padding; not a proposal.",
    "no_cow": "Replace mutable Health column lookup with read-only lookup. Deliberately bypasses ownership and hash invalidation, invalid for snapshots; not a proposal.",
    "known_target": "Hardcode Health archetype 0 and row target.index-1. Valid only for the benchmark initial layout; bypasses generation, death, pending-spawn, and archetype validation. Unsafe; not a proposal.",
    "serial_lookup": "Read the stable entity page table once without atomic acquire loads, validate generation, then return archetype/row. Applies only in this diagnostic serial dispatch context, not general threaded entity lookup.",
    "membership": "Estimate row as target.index minus first table entity.index. Bounds-check, verify exact index+generation against the table entity column, and accept that archetype/row only on equality; otherwise call authoritative tide_entity_location. Safe for coherent worlds and preserves ordering. Restricted in production to one admitted archetype across per-entity handlers."
  },
  "outcome": "Initial ablations showed no safe measured event improvement: switch ordering, queue zeroing, COW checks, and serial lookup overlapped baseline. The unsafe hardcoded-row ablation identified target mapping as substantial overhead. A later bounds-checked table-membership probe with exact index+generation equality and authoritative fallback then delivered a repeatable improvement and was implemented in production; details follow.",
  "limits": "All diagnostics agreed on the benchmark final-state digest; that does not validate snapshot or event semantics for ablations that deliberately bypass guarantees. C timings varied too (roughly 0.12-0.18 ms); phase ranges are evidence about bottlenecks, not precise cross-run percentage speedups. Programs and runs were sequential with no concurrent agent builds/tests/benchmarks.",
